# the wheel in a scroll view (ui/list.rs): a notch scrolls the system's lines of 16 DIP
# (ui.wheel_lines: Windows' mouse settings, KDE's; three in a headless run), smoothly; a page
# with plat::WHEEL_PAGE; a touchpad's pixels (a trackpad's WHEEL_PIXELS, Windows' fine steps
# WHEEL_FINE) at once, the fine steps' fractions adding up
size 900 620
expect #7000 value 0
wheel "Bereiche" -120
wait 400
expect #7000 value 48
system env jfgui_WHEEL_LINES 5
system settings other
wheel "Bereiche" -120
wait 400
expect #7000 value 128
# a trackpad: its pixels, at once (no wait)
wheel "Bereiche" -30 pixels
expect #7000 value 158
wheel "Bereiche" 8 pixels
expect #7000 value 150
# a precision touchpad on Windows: three fine steps of 40 are a notch, five lines of 16 DIP
wheel "Bereiche" -40 fine
wheel "Bereiche" -40 fine
wheel "Bereiche" -40 fine
expect #7000 value 230
# a page a notch: the view's height (548 DIP), half of it for half a notch
system env jfgui_WHEEL_LINES page
system settings other
wheel "Bereiche" 1200
wait 400
expect #7000 value 0
wheel "Bereiche" -60
wait 400
expect #7000 value 274
wheel "Bereiche" 1200
wait 400
system env jfgui_WHEEL_LINES -
system settings other
wheel "Bereiche" -120
wait 400
expect #7000 value 48
